{"text": " Is there a way to tell your future self what your dreams and plans actually were? Because most of it gets forgotten. Not the big ones, the specifics, what you wanted when you wanted it by and why it mattered at the time. That is what Demia is for. You write down what you intend to do. It gets today's date. It goes into a public archive. It stays there. Phase one is live now. That is the writing it down part. It will not remind you. It will not track your progress. That is phase two and it is not built yet. What phase one gives you is one thing. In five years, there is a dated record of what you said in your own words that you can go back and check. Demia.com. Write one down today.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 5.04, "text": " Is there a way to tell your future self what your dreams and plans actually were?", "tokens": [50363, 1148, 612, 257, 835, 284, 1560, 534, 2003, 2116, 644, 534, 10625, 290, 3352, 1682, 547, 30, 50643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17855047775527177, "compression_ratio": 1.6639676113360324, "no_speech_prob": 0.0052213044837117195, "words": [{"word": " Is", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.18, "probability": 0.8899247646331787}, {"word": " there", "start": 0.18, "end": 0.32, "probability": 0.995266318321228}, {"word": " a", "start": 0.32, "end": 0.48, "probability": 0.9941521286964417}, {"word": " way", "start": 0.48, "end": 0.6, "probability": 0.9985077977180481}, {"word": " to", "start": 0.6, "end": 0.82, "probability": 0.9962463974952698}, {"word": " tell", "start": 0.82, "end": 1.0, "probability": 0.9980837106704712}, {"word": " your", "start": 1.0, "end": 1.2, "probability": 0.9904224872589111}, {"word": " future", "start": 1.2, "end": 1.54, "probability": 0.9911627769470215}, {"word": " self", "start": 1.54, "end": 1.96, "probability": 0.9464694261550903}, {"word": " what", "start": 1.96, "end": 2.74, "probability": 0.6340231895446777}, {"word": " your", "start": 2.74, "end": 2.98, "probability": 0.99116